n","- Simple text datasets.\n","- Logs.\n","- Large unstructured text files.\n","\n","For sophisticated RAG systems, other strategies often provide better boundaries.\n","\n","## Sentence-Based Chunking\n","\n","Sentence-based chunking splits text according to sentence boundaries.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```\n","Sentence 1: Machine learning is a subset of AI.\n","Sentence 2: It learns patterns from data.\n","Sentence 3: Supervised learning uses labeled data.\n","Sentence 4: Unsupervised learning uses unlabeled data.\n","```\n","\n","You could group two sentences per chunk.\n","\n","```\n","Chunk 1:\n","Machine learning is a subset of AI.\n","It learns patterns from data.\n","\n","Chunk 2:\n","Supervised learning uses labeled data.\n","Unsupervised learning uses unlabeled data.\n","```\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"de045e42","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.780075Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.779552Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.785485Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.784653Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.011939,"end_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.787191+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.775252+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["import re\n","\n","def sentence_chunking(text, chunk_size=3, overlap=1):\n","    if chunk_size <= 0 or overlap < 0 or overlap >= chunk_size:\n","        raise ValueError(\"Invalid chunk_size or overlap\")\n","\n","    sentences = re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', text.strip())\n","\n","    chunks = []\n","    step = chunk_size - overlap\n","\n","    for i in range(0, len(sentences), step):\n","        chunk = \" \".join(sentences[i:i + chunk_size])\n","        chunks.append(chunk)\n","\n","    return chunks"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"24b92098","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.795337Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.794743Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.80008Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.79922Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.011536,"end_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.801896+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.79036+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Chunk 1:\n","Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence. It allows systems to learn from data. Deep learning uses neural networks.\n","\n"]}],"source":["chunks = sentence_chunking(\n","    text,\n","    chunk_size=100,\n","    overlap=20\n",")\n","\n","for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):\n","    print(f\"Chunk {i + 1}:\")\n","    print(chunk)\n","    print()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"ed58ee57","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.809779Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.809479Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.81513Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.814347Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.012028,"end_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.817132+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.805104+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Chunk 1:\n","Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence.\n","It allows systems to learn from data.\n","Deep learning uses neural networks.\n","\n"]}],"source":["from langchain_text_splitters import (\n","    RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\n",")\n","\n","splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(\n","    separators=[\"\\n\\n\", \"\\n\", \". \", \" \"],\n","    chunk_size=500,\n","    chunk_overlap=50\n",")\n","\n","chunks = splitter.split_text(text)\n","\n","for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):\n","    print(f\"Chunk {i + 1}:\")\n","    print(chunk)\n","    print()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ec65e091","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.003206,"end_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.823642+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.820436+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Advantages**\n","\n","- Preserves sentence boundaries.\n","- More natural than fixed character splitting.\n","- Simple and lightweight.\n","\n","**Disadvantages**\n","\n","- Sentence lengths vary.\n","- Some sentences are extremely long.\n","- Does not necessarily preserve topic boundaries.\n","\n","Note: The regex above is a simple demonstration. Real sentence segmentation should account for abbreviations, decimal points, multilingual text, and other cases.\n","\n","## Recursive Character Text Splitting\n","\n","Very popular in LangChain\n","\n","Recursive chunking is one of the most commonly used approaches in practical RAG systems.\n","\n","The idea is:\n","\n","Try to split text using the largest meaningful separators first. If the resulting pieces are too large, recursively split them using smaller separators.\n","\n","For example, a separator hierarchy could be:\n","\n","```\n","1. Paragraph separator: \\n\\n\n","2. Line separator: \\n\n","3. Sentence separator: .\n","4. Word separator: space\n","5. Character separator: \"\"\n","```\n","\n","The splitting logic tries to preserve larger text structures before resorting to smaller units.\n","\n","Suppose you have:\n","\n","```\n","Section 1:\n","Machine learning is a subset of AI.\n","\n","Section 2:\n","Supervised learning uses labeled data.\n","\n","Section 3:\n","Unsupervised learning discovers patterns.\n","```\n","\n","If the entire text exceeds the chunk size:\n","\n","1. Split on paragraph boundaries.\n","2. If a paragraph is too large, split by sentences.\n","3. If a sentence is too large, split by words.\n","4. If necessary, split by characters.\n","\n","![Recursive Splitting](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/recursive_splitting.png)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"9e7a3a04","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.83205Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.831709Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.841156Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.840252Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.016227,"end_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.843145+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.826918+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def recursive_character_chunking(\n","    text,\n","    chunk_size=100,\n","    overlap=20,\n","    separators=None\n","):\n","    if separators is None:\n","        separators = [\"\\n\\n\", \"\\n\", \" \", \"\"]\n","\n","    if chunk_size <= 0 or overlap < 0 or overlap >= chunk_size:\n","        raise ValueError(\"Invalid chunk_size or overlap\")\n","\n","    # Base case\n","    if len(text) <= chunk_size:\n","        return [text] if text else []\n","\n","    separator = separators[0]\n","\n","    # Split text using current separator\n","    if separator:\n","        splits = text.split(separator)\n","    else:\n","        splits = list(text)\n","\n","    chunks = []\n","    current_chunk = \"\"\n","\n","    for split in splits:\n","        if not split:\n","            continue\n","\n","        candidate = (\n","            current_chunk + separator + split\n","            if current_chunk else split\n","        )\n","\n","        if len(candidate) <= chunk_size:\n","            current_chunk = candidate\n","\n","        else:\n","            if current_chunk:\n","                chunks.append(current_chunk)\n","\n","            if len(split) > chunk_size:\n","                if len(separators) > 1:\n","                    chunks.extend(\n","                        recursive_character_chunking(\n","                            split,\n","                            chunk_size,\n","                            overlap,\n","                            separators[1:]\n","                        )\n","                    )\n","                else:\n","                    chunks.extend([\n","                        split[i:i + chunk_size]\n","                        for i in range(0, len(split), chunk_size)\n","                    ])\n","\n","                current_chunk = \"\"\n","            else:\n","                current_chunk = split\n","\n","    if current_chunk:\n","        chunks.append(current_chunk)\n","\n","    # Apply overlap between chunks\n","    if overlap > 0 and len(chunks) > 1:\n","        overlapped_chunks = [chunks[0]]\n","\n","        for i in range(1, len(chunks)):\n","            previous = chunks[i - 1]\n","            current = chunks[i]\n","\n","            overlapped_chunks.append(\n","                previous[-overlap:] + current\n","            )\n","\n","        chunks = overlapped_chunks\n","\n","    return chunks"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"485d4f8e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.852757Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.852075Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.857787Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.85671Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.012204,"end_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.859694+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.84749+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Chunk 1:\n","Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence.\n","It allows systems to learn from data.\n","\n","Chunk 2:\n"," to learn from data. to learn from data.Deep learning uses neural networks.\n","\n"]}],"source":["chunks = recursive_character_chunking(\n","    text,\n","    chunk_size=100,\n","    overlap=20\n",")\n","\n","for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks):\n","    print(f\"Chunk {i + 1}:\")\n","    print(chunk)\n","    print()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"a0b00787","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.86844Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.868069Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.874099Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T18:51:56.873173Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.0